      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIR JIMMY (10) went back last start and failed to really threaten when 3.5 metres from the winner in second at this track over 2240m. That effort followed a win at this track two runs ago. Draws out a little on the second line and may need luck at some point. Not disgraced last time. Good enough to take out a race like this. SMOKEN ACE NZ (8) has been a bit hot and cold and that continued last start when he finished second, beaten 1.1 metres, in a nice return to form at Menangle over 1609m. Will enjoy a pretty soft run from this draw, with the sprint lane to play a big role. Meets a similar line up so he is capable of taking this out. CATCH A WAVE (7) is in the mix following a sixth at his most recent appearance over 1720m at this track. BULLETPROOF BOY (12) comes here following a Group One sixth four months ago over 2936m at Gloucester Park, beaten 8 metres by Magnificent Storm. Top-shelf performer who is nicely placed to return in style.",
